  "stage": {
    "routeId": "camino-frances",
    "index": 18,
    "count": 33,
    "name": "Bercianos del Real Camino to Mansilla de las Mulas",
    "theme": "Endlessness",
    "narrative": "The last stage of the meseta, and it knows it. The flatness that once terrified you has become a companion. You walk toward Mansilla de las Mulas across land so level you can see the town for an hour before you reach it. The medieval walls still stand. Tomorrow you will be in León, and the meseta will be behind you. Many pilgrims feel a strange sadness here — the emptiness they dreaded has become the space where they found themselves, and they are about to lose it.",
    "closing": "What will you miss about the emptiness when it is gone?",
